A||||11||Axmanmkii||Okay, now I'm drooling over these cars, but...||||1||
Z||000000||Axmanmkii||12-29-2001||11:22 AM||||What the heck do I look at when I expect a use Fiero? I know all the obviouse stuff such as rust, belts, tires, ect.<P>But does the Fiero have a nasty surprise you should always look for? From my browse of this Forum, the Fiero is a pretty reliable car if you dont wreck it.||||reg||1
Z||000001||The Fieromaster||12-29-2001||11:26 AM||||Look for the average engine running concerns.. Smoking out exhaust, loud thuds from block  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">, rust in the TRUNK under the carpet where the 2 step ups are... Thats a big one!!  Also headlight motor problems arent a big concern... its a Fiero thing.. if they grind when they go down its no biggie!<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">          <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">     <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">      <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Fastback, Black and Yellow Interior, Planning 4G63 Turbo DSM swap for it!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Axmanmkii||12-29-2001||11:28 AM||||Hey Fieromaster, I see you're a DSM guy!<P>Not that I'm calling you out, it's just nice to see something familiar in a foreign land. Even though I'm too poor to afford a real DSM, but I love my GS alot.<P>Okay, enough O/T.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TRiAD||12-29-2001||11:53 AM||||Something hard to look for, but it's COMMON. <P>Failing/failed clutch master and/or slave cylinders. <P>I bought my car in October, drove it like 250 miles home, got about another 150 miles in it or so, and whammo. It's been parked ever since. <P>Best of luck. <BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://centralillinoisimports.org/uploads/files/SigRear4.gif">  <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||12-29-2001||11:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Axmanmkii:<BR><B>Hey Fieromaster, I see you're a DSM guy!<P>Not that I'm calling you out, it's just nice to see something familiar in a foreign land. Even though I'm too poor to afford a real DSM, but I love my GS alot.<P>Okay, enough O/T.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Dont worry your still a DSM guy because you have a GS... lol!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> dont worry! Heck NOW you can be a Fiero guy too!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TTiger||12-29-2001||12:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Axmanmkii:<BR><B> I know all the obviouse stuff such as rust, belts, tires, ect.<P>But does the Fiero have a nasty surprise you should always look for? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You mentioned the rust, but make sure you lift the carpet in the "trunk" by the engine compartment.  The rust under there can be a very big nasty, expensive surprise for you after you buy it.<P>Tony<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttigersig_21.gif"> <P>||||reg||14
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||12-29-2001||12:30 PM||||I like DSMs too.. I'd prefer to be a Supra guy though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (but I sure wouldn't turn down a nice Talon!)<P>Anyway, look for rust in the rear frame area, peel back the trunk carpeting to check for rust there, behind the battery tray, etc. Some cosmetic stuff, like the edges of the dash being chipped away, edges of the console peeling.. hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000007||Axmanmkii||12-29-2001||03:32 PM||||Is there anyway to check the cluch master and slave cylinders, besides haveing it break down?||||reg||1
Z||000008||88CoupeV6||12-29-2001||03:37 PM||||If the clutch releases good and the clutch pedal feel fine it should be OK, If your clutch releases on the floor there may be a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Axmanmkii||12-29-2001||03:43 PM||||Wow, not that many hidden problems, compare to a SHO that is.<P>Well, hopefully there's a Fiero left in the world for me. Wish me luck!||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroBUZZ||12-29-2001||06:19 PM||||Look at lots of cars and go for the very best car you can afford.  I sent my first three of to the junkyard. A lot of the cosmetic stuff, like seats, dashes and all are easy to fix. Clutch and rust problems are forever. The fix me uppers turn into money pits pretty quick.<P>On V-6's don't forget to watch for leaky exhaust manifolds.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroHarry||12-30-2001||09:47 AM||||Always look at the stainless tubes running under the doors. I have seen plenty of cars lifted the wrong way and these can get crushed easily. Could lead to expensive replacement's down the road...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SIg1_2.jpg"> <B>"If you want to blend in, take the bus!"</B>||||reg||1
